  "rendered": "According to the 2022 cobalt-free review, the total usable cobalt from known global cobalt reserves is approximately 2 million metric tons, assuming a conservative mining efficiency of 70% and cobalt directed toward battery manufacturing industries to be 40%.\n\nThe 2020 NFA paper estimates that one fleet of one million EVs with NMC 111 cathodes would require approximately 2500 tons of cobalt.\n\nTo calculate how many fleets of one million EVs with NMC 111 cathodes the usable cobalt reserves could supply, we can divide the total usable cobalt by the cobalt required for one fleet:\n\n2,000,000 metric tons (usable cobalt) ÷ 2500 tons (cobalt per fleet) = 800 fleets",
